    <div class="key"><span class="hit">Division with a company</span><span>No company yet</span><span class="note">IBM (3570) would sit in D, but 3570 is not in the hierarchy</span></div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="h-co">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 id="h-co">Each company against the hierarchy</h2>
      <p class="lede">The code is joined to <code>sic_code</code>, then the two descriptions are compared. EDGAR writes its own wording, so a match on code does not mean identical text.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Company</th><th>CIK</th><th>SIC</th><th>EDGAR wording</th><th>Hierarchy wording</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Apple Inc.</td><td class="mono num">0000320193</td><td class="mono">3571</td><td>Electronic Computers</td><td>Electronic Computers</td><td><span class="pill good">Identical</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Ford Motor Co</td><td class="mono num">0000037996</td><td class="mono">3711</td><td>Motor Vehicles &amp; Passenger Car Bodies</td><td>Motor Vehicles and Passenger Car Bodies</td><td><span class="pill info">Wording differs</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Tesla, Inc.</td><td class="mono num">0001318605</td><td class="mono">3711</td><td>Motor Vehicles &amp; Passenger Car Bodies</td><td>Motor Vehicles and Passenger Car Bodies</td><td><span class="pill info">Wording differs</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Oracle Corp</td><td class="mono num">0001341439</td><td class="mono">7372</td><td>Services-Prepackaged Software</td><td>Prepackaged Software</td><td><span class="pill info">Wording differs</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Target Corp</td><td class="mono num">0000027419</td><td class="mono">5331</td><td>Retail-Variety Stores</td><td>Variety Stores</td><td><span class="pill info">Wording differs</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Walmart Inc.</td><td class="mono num">0000104169</td><td class="mono">5331</td><td>Retail-Variety Stores</td><td>Variety Stores</td><td><span class="pill info">Wording differs</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>International Business Machines Corp</td><td class="mono num">0000051143</td><td class="mono">3570</td><td>Computer &amp; office Equipment</td><td>No row for 3570</td><td><span class="pill warn">No parent code</span></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="h-dq">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 id="h-dq">Data quality and what to do with it</h2>
      <p class="lede">The result of <code>RUN DQ</code> on <code>company</code>, followed by what the numbers mean.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="two">
      <div class="tbl-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Column</th><th>Rule</th><th class="r">Checked</th><th class="r">Valid</th><th class="r">Invalid</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td class="mono">cik</td><td>Primary key</td><td class="r num">7</td><td class="r num">7</td><td class="r num">0</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="mono">sic</td><td>Foreign key to <code>sic_code</code></td><td class="r num">7</td><td class="r num">6</td><td class="r num"><b style="color:var(--orange)">1</b></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <ul class="finds">
        <li><b>IBM fails because its code is missing, not because the data is wrong.</b><span>EDGAR files IBM under SIC 3570. The hierarchy lists 3571 and its neighbours but not 3570. Adding that one row to <code>sic_code</code> would clear the failure.</span></li>
        <li><b>The older profile view hides this gap; the USL shows it.</b><span><code>edgar.all_companies_profile_table</code> joins the same two sources and silently drops IBM, so it has 6 rows. The USL keeps all 7 and flags the one that does not resolve.</span></li>
        <li><b>The object store holds all 7 companies.</b><span>The materialization used <code>recordType = 'all'</code>, so IBM is in the Parquet file. Writing only rows that pass the checks needs <code>'valid'</code>, which has not been tried.</span></li>
        <li><b>Five of the six matches use different wording.</b><span>EDGAR prefixes the division (&ldquo;Services-&rdquo;) and writes &ldquo;&amp;&rdquo;, while the hierarchy spells out &ldquo;and&rdquo;. A key check passes these, so compare text separately if wording matters.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

