  <section aria-labelledby="h-recipe">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 id="h-recipe">Recipe: repeat this at your site</h2>
      <p class="lede">Fifteen steps from an unpacked package to a verified Parquet object in a bucket on {{STORE_NAME}}, ending with the report to send back, a troubleshooting table and the cleanup. Each step has the command to copy and the output to expect. Replace anything in angle brackets with your own value. Values such as timestamps, ids and file names will differ.</p>
    </div>

    <ol class="steps">

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Check what you need</h3>
        <div class="body">
          <ul>
            <li>Zetaris Lightning 2.4.3.1 or later, running, with JDBC on port 10000 and the REST API on port 8888, and a user that can create USLs and storage settings.</li>
            <li>The Zetaris JDBC driver JAR, and a JDK 11 or later (JDK 17 was used).</li>
            <li>Python 3.10 or later.</li>
            <li>An API key you create yourself in the Zetaris GUI (the scripts never create one).</li>
            <li>For {{STORE_NAME}}: the S3 endpoint URL, an access key, a secret key and an existing bucket.</li>
            <li>The package, unzipped. It holds <code>systems/</code>, <code>scripts/</code>, <code>open_data/</code> and <code>docs/</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Create the Python environment</h3>
        <div class="body">
          <p>From the package folder:</p>
          <div class="code"><button class="copy" type="button" data-target="c-venv">Copy</button><pre id="c-venv">cd &lt;package folder&gt;
python3 -m venv .venv
.venv/bin/pip install -r systems/object_stores/requirements.txt</pre></div>
          <div class="callout-box info"><b>Expect</b> no errors. The venv gives the scripts <code>jaydebeapi</code> for JDBC. The scripts find a Homebrew JDK on macOS by themselves.</div>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Put your settings in .env.local</h3>
        <div class="body">
          <p>Copy <code>systems/object_stores/.env.example</code> to <code>.env.local</code> in the package folder (<code>cp systems/object_stores/.env.example .env.local</code>) and fill it in. Every script reads the keys from it without printing them. Do not put <code>.env.local</code> in a ZIP you share. Never paste keys into a prompt, a chat or a commit.</p>
          <div class="code"><button class="copy" type="button" data-target="c-env">Copy</button><pre id="c-env"># Zetaris
ZETARIS_USERNAME=&lt;your Zetaris user id&gt;
ZETARIS_PASSWORD=&lt;your Zetaris password&gt;
ZETARIS_API_KEY=&lt;API key created in the Zetaris GUI&gt;
ZETARIS_USER_AGENT=&lt;app name&gt; &lt;contact email&gt;
ZETARIS_JDBC_JAR=/full/path/to/ndp-jdbc-driver-&lt;version&gt;-driver.jar

# S3-compatible object store
S3_ENDPOINT_URL=https://&lt;your S3 endpoint&gt;
S3_ACCESS_KEY=&lt;access key&gt;
S3_SECRET_KEY=&lt;secret key&gt;
S3_BUCKET=&lt;bucket name&gt;
S3_PREFIX=&lt;your own folder, for example jane-usl-test&gt;</pre></div>
          <div class="callout-box info"><b>Note</b> <code>ZETARIS_USER_AGENT</code> is sent to the public SEC EDGAR API, which asks callers to identify themselves. Use a real contact. The REST URL defaults to <code>http://localhost:8888/api/v1.0</code> and the organization id to <code>1</code>, so a local install needs nothing more.</div>
          <div class="callout-box info"><b>Optional</b> Three more settings adapt the scripts to a store that behaves differently: <code>S3_ADDRESSING</code> (<code>path</code> or <code>virtual</code>), <code>S3_REGION</code> and <code>S3_CA_BUNDLE</code> (a PEM file, for a private certificate authority). Leave them out until the probe in step 8 says otherwise.</div>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Run the preflight</h3>
        <div class="body">
          <p>Read-only. It checks the settings, REST, Java, the venv, the JAR, a JDBC <code>SELECT 1</code> and, with <code>--s3</code>, the object store settings. It makes no call to the store; the probe in step 8 does that.</p>
          <div class="code"><button class="copy" type="button" data-target="c-pre">Copy</button><pre id="c-pre">python3 scripts/preflight.py --jdbc --s3</pre></div>
          <div class="code out"><span class="lbl">Expected output</span><pre><span class="pass">[PASS]</span> env file: &lt;package&gt;/.env.local
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> ZETARIS_API_KEY: set
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> ZETARIS_USERNAME: set
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> ZETARIS_PASSWORD: set
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> ZETARIS_USER_AGENT: set, in the form app_name user@domain.tld
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> REST datasources: HTTP 200, 0 listed: 
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> REST SELECT 1
[INFO] datasources: none
[INFO] lightning databases: &lt;your databases&gt;
[INFO] USL namespaces: none
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> JDBC port 10000: open
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> Java (JDK 11+): /opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk@17/libexec/openjdk.jdk/Contents/Home
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> .venv: &lt;package&gt;/.venv/bin/python
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> jaydebeapi: importable
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> driver JAR: /full/path/to/ndp-jdbc-driver-&lt;version&gt;-driver.jar
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> JDBC SELECT 1
[INFO] datasources: none
[INFO] lightning databases: &lt;your databases&gt;
[INFO] USL namespaces: none
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> S3_ENDPOINT_URL: set
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> S3_BUCKET: set
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> S3_ACCESS_KEY: set
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> S3_SECRET_KEY: set
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> S3_ADDRESSING: path
[INFO] S3_CA_BUNDLE: not set (the CA file Python trusts is used)
<span class="okc">READY</span></pre></div>
          <div class="callout-box info"><b>Note</b> The three INFO lines show what is already on the instance. They appear twice, once after the REST checks and once after the JDBC check, and your lists will differ.</div>
          <div class="callout-box">If you see <b>NOT READY</b>, fix the line marked FAIL first. Every later step assumes READY.</div>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Onboard the sources and build the USL</h3>
        <div class="body">
          <p>Show the plan first. Nothing is sent.</p>
          <div class="code"><button class="copy" type="button" data-target="c-dry">Copy</button><pre id="c-dry">python3 scripts/onboard.py run sic_edgar_usl --channel jdbc --dry-run</pre></div>
          <div class="code out"><span class="lbl">Expected output</span><pre> 1. company_dns      rest  open_data/rest_apis/sql/rate_limited/12_company_dns_create.sql
 2. edgar_facts      rest  open_data/rest_apis/sql/rate_limited/01_edgar_company_facts_create.sql
 3. edgar_profiles   rest  open_data/rest_apis/sql/rate_limited/11_edgar_company_profiles_create.sql
 4. sic_edgar_usl    usl   open_data/usl/sql/02_sic_edgar_usl_create.sql
<span class="dim">(dry run: nothing sent)</span></pre></div>
          <p>Then run it. This creates objects on the instance and calls the public APIs once, so run it once and deliberately.</p>
          <div class="code"><button class="copy" type="button" data-target="c-onb">Copy</button><pre id="c-onb">python3 scripts/onboard.py run sic_edgar_usl --channel jdbc</pre></div>
          <div class="code out"><span class="lbl">Expected output</span><pre>=== company_dns (10 statements, dependency)
    <span class="pass">10 ok</span>
=== edgar_facts (16 statements, dependency)
    <span class="pass">16 ok</span>
=== edgar_profiles (15 statements, dependency)
    <span class="pass">15 ok</span>
=== sic_edgar_usl (9 statements)
    <span class="pass">9 ok</span>
done</pre></div>
          <div class="callout-box info"><b>Note</b> Sources that are only pulled in as dependencies skip "already exists" by themselves, so leftovers from an earlier run do no harm. Naming a source or USL that already exists needs <code>--skip-exists</code>, otherwise the run stops at the first duplicate. The line <code>SLF4J: Failed to load class</code> is a harmless warning from the driver, which bundles no logging backend.</div>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Confirm the USL has the data</h3>
        <div class="body">
          <div class="code"><button class="copy" type="button" data-target="c-cnt">Copy</button><pre id="c-cnt">python3 scripts/run_sql.py --channel jdbc -e "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM lightning.metastore.usl_demo.sic_edgar_usl.sic_code"
python3 scripts/run_sql.py --channel jdbc -e "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM lightning.metastore.usl_demo.sic_edgar_usl.company"
python3 scripts/run_sql.py --channel jdbc -e "RUN DQ TABLE lightning.metastore.usl_demo.sic_edgar_usl.company"</pre></div>
          <div class="code out"><span class="lbl">Expected output</span><pre>[1005]
[7]
['cik', 'company', 'Primary Key Constraint', 7, 7, 0]
['sic', 'company', 'Foreign Key Constraint', 7, 6, 1]</pre></div>
          <div class="callout-box info"><b>Note</b> One foreign-key row is invalid on purpose in this data set: IBM is filed under SIC 3570, which is not in the hierarchy. It does not stop materialization.</div>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Check the helper packages</h3>
        <div class="body">
          <p>Step 2 already installed everything in <code>systems/object_stores/requirements.txt</code>: <code>jaydebeapi</code> for JDBC, <code>boto3</code> for the S3 API and <code>pyarrow</code> to read Parquet. This confirms they load.</p>
          <div class="code"><button class="copy" type="button" data-target="c-pip">Copy</button><pre id="c-pip">.venv/bin/python -c "import jaydebeapi, boto3, pyarrow; print('helpers ok')"</pre></div>
          <div class="code out"><span class="lbl">Expected output</span><pre><span class="pass">helpers ok</span></pre></div>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Probe the object store before touching Zetaris</h3>
        <div class="body">
          <p>This tests the endpoint, the keys and the bucket, and tries your configured addressing style and region first, then the other style and three region names. It writes one tiny test object under <code>&lt;your folder&gt;/zetaris-probe/</code>, deletes it, and creates your own folder in the bucket. Everything this test writes goes under that folder, which is <code>S3_PREFIX</code> or <code>usl-test-</code> plus your login name, so people who share a bucket do not collide. Add <code>--no-write</code> to stay read-only.</p>
          <div class="code"><button class="copy" type="button" data-target="c-probe">Copy</button><pre id="c-probe">.venv/bin/python systems/object_stores/scripts/probe_s3.py</pre></div>
          <div class="code out"><span class="lbl">Expected output</span><pre>endpoint=https://&lt;endpoint&gt; bucket=&lt;bucket&gt; tls_verify=&lt;CA file&gt;
configured: addressing=path region=us-east-1
your folder: s3://&lt;bucket&gt;/&lt;your folder&gt;/
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> style=path    region=us-east-1  head_bucket + list ok
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> style=path    region=us-west-2  head_bucket + list ok
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> style=path    region=eu-west-1  head_bucket + list ok
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> style=virtual region=us-east-1  head_bucket + list ok
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> style=virtual region=us-west-2  head_bucket + list ok
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> style=virtual region=eu-west-1  head_bucket + list ok

Your configured settings work: S3_ADDRESSING=path S3_REGION=us-east-1

Write test with style=path region=us-east-1: &lt;your folder&gt;/zetaris-probe/&lt;uuid&gt;.txt
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> put_object
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> get_object matches
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> delete_object
<span class="pass">[PASS]</span> your folder s3://&lt;bucket&gt;/&lt;your folder&gt;/ created</pre></div>
          <div class="callout-box"><b>If every line fails with CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED:</b> the endpoint's certificate chain may be public, but boto3's bundled CA list may not include its root. The scripts already use the CA file your Python trusts. If your endpoint uses a private CA, set <code>S3_CA_BUNDLE</code> in <code>.env.local</code> or pass <code>--ca-bundle /path/to/ca.pem</code>. Do not turn verification off.</div>
          <div class="callout-box info"><b>What this tells you</b> The line after the table says whether your configured settings work. If not, copy the <code>S3_ADDRESSING</code> and <code>S3_REGION</code> it prints into <code>.env.local</code> and run the probe again. The probe runs on your machine, so it does not prove that the Zetaris engine can reach the store or trust its certificate chain. The materialize step is the real test.</div>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Create the storage setting in Zetaris</h3>
        <div class="body">
          <p>There is no SQL statement to create a storage setting, so this calls the REST endpoint <code>POST /storage-setting</code>. Look at the request first, with the keys hidden:</p>
          <div class="code"><button class="copy" type="button" data-target="c-ss1">Copy</button><pre id="c-ss1">.venv/bin/python systems/object_stores/scripts/storage_setting.py create --dry-run</pre></div>
          <div class="code out"><span class="lbl">Expected output</span><pre>POST /storage-setting (dry run, nothing sent)
{
  "storageName": "s3-compat-&lt;your folder&gt;",
  "storageType": "S3",
  "storagePath": "s3a://&lt;bucket&gt;/&lt;your folder&gt;",
  "scope": "Owner",
  "config": {
    "awsAccessKeyId": "&lt;redacted&gt;",
    "awsSecretAccessKey": "&lt;redacted&gt;",
    "s3Endpoint": "https://&lt;endpoint&gt;",
    "useS3PathStyleAccess": "true"
  }
}</pre></div>
          <p>With <code>S3_ADDRESSING=virtual</code> the <code>useS3PathStyleAccess</code> line is left out. Create it, then note the id it returns:</p>
          <div class="code"><button class="copy" type="button" data-target="c-ss2">Copy</button><pre id="c-ss2">.venv/bin/python systems/object_stores/scripts/storage_setting.py create
.venv/bin/python systems/object_stores/scripts/storage_setting.py list</pre></div>
          <div class="code out"><span class="lbl">Expected output</span><pre>HTTP 200
{
  "id": "&lt;storage setting id&gt;"
}</pre></div>
          <div class="callout-box"><b>Creating a setting does not test it.</b> It is accepted even if the endpoint or keys are wrong. The real test is the materialize step. Use <code>storage_setting.py delete &lt;id&gt;</code> to remove one. The setting is named <code>s3-compat-</code> plus your folder, so each person has their own. If you get <code>HTTP 400</code> and <code>already exists</code>, pass another name with <code>--name</code>.</div>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Materialize the USL tables with SQL</h3>
        <div class="body">
          <p>The script builds the statement from <code>.env.local</code>. Dry-run first. It masks the credentials in what it prints.</p>
          <div class="code"><button class="copy" type="button" data-target="c-mat1">Copy</button><pre id="c-mat1">.venv/bin/python systems/object_stores/scripts/materialize_usl_table.py \
  lightning.metastore.usl_demo.sic_edgar_usl.sic_code \
  --setting-id &lt;storage setting id&gt; --variant options-json --dry-run</pre></div>
          <div class="code out"><span class="lbl">Expected output</span><pre>MATERIALIZE USL TABLE lightning.metastore.usl_demo.sic_edgar_usl.sic_code TO STORAGE (
  recordType = 'all',
  path = 's3a://&lt;bucket&gt;/&lt;your folder&gt;/usl_demo/sic_edgar_usl/sic_code',
  format = 'parquet',
  storageSettingId = '&lt;storage setting id&gt;',
  optionsBase64 = '&lt;base64 JSON with credentials&gt;'
)

<span class="dim">(dry run: nothing sent)</span></pre></div>
          <p>Run it for both tables:</p>
          <div class="code"><button class="copy" type="button" data-target="c-mat2">Copy</button><pre id="c-mat2">.venv/bin/python systems/object_stores/scripts/materialize_usl_table.py \
  lightning.metastore.usl_demo.sic_edgar_usl.sic_code \
  --setting-id &lt;storage setting id&gt; --variant options-json

.venv/bin/python systems/object_stores/scripts/materialize_usl_table.py \
  lightning.metastore.usl_demo.sic_edgar_usl.company \
  --setting-id &lt;storage setting id&gt; --variant options-json</pre></div>
          <div class="code out"><span class="lbl">Expected output (last line of each run)</span><pre>RESULT: s3a://&lt;bucket&gt;/&lt;your folder&gt;/usl_demo/sic_edgar_usl/sic_code | <span class="pass">SUCCESS</span> | None | None
RESULT: s3a://&lt;bucket&gt;/&lt;your folder&gt;/usl_demo/sic_edgar_usl/company | <span class="pass">SUCCESS</span> | None | None</pre></div>
          <div class="callout-box"><b>The credentials must be inside the options.</b> The manual's example passes only <code>storageSettingId</code>. On Zetaris 2.4.3.1 that failed with <code>NoAuthWithAWSException: No AWS Credentials provided</code>, and so did extra top-level keys and <code>fs.s3a.*</code> names. It worked once the S3 keys, endpoint and <code>useS3PathStyleAccess</code> went into the <code>optionsBase64</code> JSON, which is what <code>--variant options-json</code> does. The statement therefore carries your keys, and the instance may keep it in query history, so use a key you can rotate. The details are in <code>systems/object_stores/issues/ISSUE-01-materialize-ignores-storage-setting.md</code>.</div>
          <div class="callout-box info"><b>Running it again</b> A second run replaces each table's output; it does not append (tested on Zetaris 2.4.3.1 with both tables: the object count and the row count were the same after a second run). Clear your folder (the last step) when you want to remove files from earlier runs that this run no longer writes.</div>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Verify the whole chain</h3>
        <div class="body">
          <p>This lists the bucket, then checks both tables from the source API through the view and the USL to the Parquet files. It is read-only and exits with 0 only when every stage matches.</p>
          <div class="code"><button class="copy" type="button" data-target="c-ver">Copy</button><pre id="c-ver">.venv/bin/python systems/object_stores/scripts/verify_chain.py</pre></div>
          <div class="code out"><span class="lbl">Expected output (stage lines)</span><pre>=== sic_code: company-dns API &gt; view &gt; USL &gt; Parquet
1a company-dns API V3 (live)                      1,005  <span class="pass">PASS</span>  reference count
1b company-dns API V4 (live)                      1,005  <span class="pass">PASS</span>
3  SchemaStore view sic_codes_table               1,005  <span class="pass">PASS</span>
4  USL table sic_code                             1,005  <span class="pass">PASS</span>
5  Parquet  &lt;your folder&gt;/usl_demo/sic_edgar_usl/sic_code  1,005  <span class="pass">PASS</span>
   USL rows vs Parquet rows (8 columns)                  <span class="pass">PASS</span>  identical

=== company: SEC EDGAR API &gt; raw tables &gt; view &gt; USL &gt; Parquet
1  SEC EDGAR submissions API (live)                   7  <span class="pass">PASS</span>
3  SchemaStore view all_companies_profile_table       6  <span class="pass">PASS</span>  omits 1 company with SIC not in sic_code
4  USL table company                                  7  <span class="pass">PASS</span>
5  Parquet  &lt;your folder&gt;/usl_demo/sic_edgar_usl/company  7  <span class="pass">PASS</span>
   USL rows vs Parquet rows (4 columns)                  <span class="pass">PASS</span>  identical

<span class="okc">CHAIN OK</span></pre></div>
          <p>An example of the full output is in the section above. Use <code>--table sic_code</code> or <code>--table company</code> to check one table.</p>
          <div class="callout-box info"><b>Your numbers will differ</b> if your data does. What matters is that every stage says PASS and the last line is <b>CHAIN OK</b>. A FAIL line names the stage and shows a few keys that differ, and the last line then reads <b>CHAIN BROKEN</b>.</div>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Explore the data live in this viewer</h3>
        <div class="body">
          <p>Start the small local server. It serves this page and runs read-only SQL against your instance with the credentials in <code>.env.local</code>, which never reach the browser.</p>
          <div class="code"><button class="copy" type="button" data-target="c-srv">Copy</button><pre id="c-srv">.venv/bin/python systems/object_stores/scripts/serve_viewer.py</pre></div>
          <div class="code out"><span class="lbl">Expected output</span><pre>Connected over JDBC (settings from &lt;package&gt;/.env.local).
Mode: <span class="pass">read-only</span>.  Viewer: <span class="okc">http://127.0.0.1:8765</span>   (Ctrl+C to stop)</pre></div>
          <p>Open <code>http://127.0.0.1:8765</code> and choose the <b>Live SQL</b> tab. Pick an example, or type your own, and press <b>Run query</b>. For example, this returns the 7 companies:</p>
          <div class="code"><button class="copy" type="button" data-target="c-q1">Copy</button><pre id="c-q1">SELECT cik, entity_name, sic, sic_description_edgar
FROM lightning.metastore.usl_demo.sic_edgar_usl.company
ORDER BY entity_name</pre></div>
          <div class="callout-box info"><b>Options</b> <code>--channel rest</code> uses the REST API instead of JDBC. <code>--port 9000</code> changes the port. <code>--allow-write</code> lets statements that change the instance through, so leave it off unless you mean it.</div>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>If something fails</h3>
        <div class="body">
          <div class="tbl-wrap">
            <table>
              <thead><tr><th>You see</th><th>Cause and fix</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED</code> from boto3</td><td>The CA list boto3 bundles lacks your endpoint's root. The scripts use Python's CA file by default. For a private CA set <code>S3_CA_BUNDLE</code> or pass <code>--ca-bundle</code>. Never disable verification.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Probe says <code>Your configured settings did not work, but this combination did</code></td><td>Copy the <code>S3_ADDRESSING</code> and <code>S3_REGION</code> it prints into <code>.env.local</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>The probe passes but the materialize result is an error</td><td>The probe runs on your machine and Zetaris runs elsewhere. Check that the engine host can reach the endpoint and trusts its certificate chain.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>NoAuthWithAWSException: No AWS Credentials provided</code> in the materialize result</td><td>The credentials were not inside <code>optionsBase64</code>. Use <code>--variant options-json</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Materialize result says <code>Error</code> but the command printed ok</td><td>The statement returns one row per run. Read that row: <code>SUCCESS</code> or <code>Error</code> followed by the message.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>boto3 is not installed in this Python</code>, or <code>No module named pyarrow</code></td><td>You used <code>python3</code>. Use <code>.venv/bin/python</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Set ZETARIS_USER_AGENT</code></td><td>Add an app name and a contact email to <code>.env.local</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>MISSING ... S3_*</code></td><td>Add the missing name to <code>.env.local</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Unable to locate a Java Runtime</code></td><td>macOS stub. Install a JDK, for example <code>brew install openjdk@17</code>; the scripts find it.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>REST <code>401</code> on <code>storage_setting.py</code></td><td>The API key is missing, wrong or expired. Create a new key in the Zetaris GUI and update <code>.env.local</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>The Live SQL tab says <b>Not connected</b></td><td>The viewer server is not running, or you opened the file directly. Run <code>.venv/bin/python systems/object_stores/scripts/serve_viewer.py</code> and use the address it prints.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>SLF4J: Failed to load class StaticLoggerBinder</code></td><td>Harmless. The driver bundles no logging backend. <code>verify_chain.py</code> and <code>serve_viewer.py</code> hide it.</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Record the run and send it back</h3>
        <div class="body">
          <p>This produces the result to send back. One command repeats the probe, the storage setting, the materialization, the chain check and the cleanup of your own folder, and writes a report. Run it before the clean up below, because it needs the USL. Before you run it, check that the preflight passes and that <code>SELECT COUNT(*) FROM lightning.metastore.usl_demo.sic_edgar_usl.company</code> returns 7. If you removed the Zetaris objects, rebuild them with step 5. The cleanup part is a dry run until you add <code>--cleanup</code>.</p>
          <div class="code"><button class="copy" type="button" data-target="c-rep">Copy</button><pre id="c-rep">.venv/bin/python systems/object_stores/scripts/report.py --cleanup</pre></div>
          <div class="code out"><span class="lbl">Expected output ends with</span><pre>Wrote reports/&lt;store&gt;-&lt;date&gt;-&lt;time&gt;.json
Wrote reports/&lt;store&gt;-&lt;date&gt;-&lt;time&gt;.md
<span class="okc">Result: PASS</span></pre></div>
          <p>The result is <b>PASS</b> (exit code 0), <b>FAIL</b> (1: a required check failed, for example the USL is missing, and the checks that depend on it were skipped with the reason), or <b>INCOMPLETE</b> (3: nothing failed, but a required check did not run, for example with <code>--store-only</code>). Exit code 2 means nothing was written because a value from <code>.env.local</code> was still in the report; send the error text, not the report. Send the <code>.json</code> and the <code>.md</code> from <code>reports/</code>. A FAIL is worth sending too.</p>
          <div class="callout-box info"><b>Safe to send</b> The report holds no keys, passwords, bucket name, endpoint, folder name, user agent or login name. Those are replaced with placeholders, and the report is not written at all if one is still found. Add <code>--store-only</code> to test just the object store, before Zetaris is involved. With this viewer server running, the newest report appears at the top of this tab by itself.</div>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Clean up</h3>
        <div class="body">
          <p>Confirm what you want gone first. These steps change the instance and the bucket. Show the Zetaris plan, read it, then run it with <code>--yes</code>:</p>
          <div class="code"><button class="copy" type="button" data-target="c-td">Copy</button><pre id="c-td">python3 scripts/onboard.py teardown sic_edgar_usl company_dns edgar_facts edgar_profiles --channel jdbc
python3 scripts/onboard.py teardown sic_edgar_usl company_dns edgar_facts edgar_profiles --channel jdbc --yes</pre></div>
          <div class="callout-box info"><b>Note</b> The REST tables, the <code>COMPANY_DNS</code> and <code>SEC_DATA</code> Lightning databases and the containers can only be removed in the Zetaris Data Explorer, and the command lists them. They do no harm if you onboard again, because dependencies skip "already exists". <code>--drop-namespace</code> also removes every other USL in <code>usl_demo</code>, so leave it off unless you want that.</div>
          <p>Delete the storage setting, then clear your own folder in the bucket. The cleanup script lists what it would delete and deletes nothing until you add <code>--yes</code>. It touches only your own folder, treats every prefix as a folder, and refuses an empty prefix, so it can never empty the whole bucket.</p>
          <div class="code"><button class="copy" type="button" data-target="c-cl">Copy</button><pre id="c-cl">.venv/bin/python systems/object_stores/scripts/storage_setting.py list
.venv/bin/python systems/object_stores/scripts/storage_setting.py delete &lt;storage setting id&gt;
.venv/bin/python systems/object_stores/scripts/cleanup_bucket.py
.venv/bin/python systems/object_stores/scripts/cleanup_bucket.py --yes</pre></div>
          <div class="code out"><span class="lbl">Expected output ends with</span><pre>Deleted. Checking again:
  &lt;your folder&gt;/  0 objects left

<span class="okc">CLEAN: every listed prefix is empty.</span></pre></div>
          <div class="callout-box">If it ends with <b>INCOMPLETE</b>, objects remain. On a versioned bucket, old versions or delete markers may need your store's console. A bucket with object lock or a retention policy refuses the deletes, and no script works around that.</div>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p class="disclaimer">Independent integration notes. Product and company names used here belong to their owners and appear only to identify the product the steps were run against; this page is not an endorsement or an official document of any of them. The example output comes from a test run against Zetaris 2.4.3.1 and may differ on other versions.</p>
  </section>
</div>

